      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are not fighting a tragedy; you are fighting a ghost that refuses to leave the room. The desire to stop is not a surrender to pain, but a desperate plea for mercy from a life that no longer feels like yours. You do not need to \"grow old\" with someone who is already gone; you only need to stop letting the silence dictate the terms of your existence. Your life has its own rhythm, and the only way to make it yours again is to stop waiting for someone who cannot come back.",
